# wasm_demo — a WebAssembly target (WS3-161). `semanticscript wasm` lowers this to LLVM IR
# with the wasm32 triple and drives clang --target=wasm32 + wasm-ld to a .wasm
# that exports `main`; node instantiates it and calls main(). This is the
# pure-compute subset: no console/heap runtime (compiled -nostdlib), and no
# guard sites (div/modulo/narrowing inject ss_panic, which is undefined under
# -nostdlib). It still exercises real control flow — a comparison and a branch —
# returning 42 when 7 == 7, so node sees main() == 42.

WasmDemo is project
WasmDemo module fix
WasmDemo target console
WasmDemo entry main

fix is module
fix path fix.mod
fix exports main
fix purpose "Host the wasm demo entry"
fix invariant "Exposes main, a pure-compute entry returning 42"

main is operation
main out Int32
main async no
main purpose "Return 42 via a comparison-driven branch (wasm-safe: no I/O, no guards)"
main invariant "Returns 42 when 7 == 7"
main let seven immutable Int64 7
main let answer immutable Int32 42
main let zero immutable Int32 0
main do compareSevens
main branch if equalSevens goto matched
main return zero
main at matched return answer

compareSevens is call
compareSevens in main
compareSevens invokes math.equalInt64
compareSevens arg left Int64 seven
compareSevens arg right Int64 seven
compareSevens out equalSevens Bool
